1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:04,969
SYMBIOTIC CITY. A self-healing urban intelligence platform — from cascading failure

2
00:00:05,019 --> 00:00:09,039
to coordinated recovery. Here is the full walkthrough.

3
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:15,664
SYMBIOTIC CITY models the fictional city of Aurora Vale. Every asset, incident and

4
00:00:15,714 --> 00:00:19,589
resident count you will see is synthetic demonstration data. The platform answers

5
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:23,515
two questions every control room asks: how far does a failure spread, and what do we

6
00:00:23,564 --> 00:00:27,439
fix first with what we have.

7
00:00:29,789 --> 00:00:32,923
Everything is protected by role-based authentication. We sign in as the City

8
00:00:32,973 --> 00:00:36,106
Operator — one of four demo roles, each with strictly different, server-enforced

9
00:00:36,156 --> 00:00:39,289
permissions.

10
00:00:41,639 --> 00:00:45,046
The dashboard is the live command surface: asset health, zone status, open incidents

11
00:00:45,096 --> 00:00:48,503
and recovery progress, all served from the platform's database. Nothing on this

12
00:00:48,553 --> 00:00:51,959
screen is mocked.

13
00:00:55,489 --> 00:00:59,991
The digital twin renders all twenty-three modelled assets and twenty-five dependency

14
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:04,542
links as an interactive 3D scene. Camera presets frame the whole city, and dragging

15
00:01:04,592 --> 00:01:09,093
orbits the view. Color is live status: operational, degraded, failed, in

16
00:01:09,143 --> 00:01:13,644
maintenance, or recovering. Selecting the Aurora Vale Generating Station opens its

17
00:01:13,694 --> 00:01:18,196
detail panel — capacity, dependencies, and the downstream assets that rely on it.

18
00:01:18,246 --> 00:01:22,747
This dependency graph is the foundation every other feature reasons about:

19
00:01:22,797 --> 00:01:27,298
simulation, optimization and the recovery workflow all read from it, so what you see

20
00:01:27,348 --> 00:01:31,849
here is exactly what the rest of the platform computes against.

21
00:01:41,689 --> 00:01:45,894
The twin is also the incident map: failed and recovering assets stand out on the

22
00:01:45,944 --> 00:01:50,149
model, and stored cascade runs can be replayed here step by step.

23
00:02:06,689 --> 00:02:10,706
Status is colour and shape — every asset carries a marker, so the model stays

24
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:14,773
readable even in monochrome. And the scene reports its own cost: meshes, draw calls,

25
00:02:14,823 --> 00:02:18,839
and frames per second. Measured, not claimed.

26
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:34,830
The infrastructure catalogue manages the same assets as data — searchable,

27
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:38,520
filterable, with categories, zones and dependency records. Every change is written

28
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:42,210
to an audit trail.

29
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:49,180
The City Copilot answers operational questions in plain language. We ask which

30
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:53,849
assets are most critical in Aurora Vale. Every reply is grounded and labelled: this

31
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:58,520
one comes from the deterministic rule engine — instant, no LLM key required. With a

32
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:03,189
Groq key configured, the same panel upgrades to large-language-model responses.

33
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:15,132
Switch to the AI Disaster Commander and the panel becomes an incident coordinator.

34
00:03:15,182 --> 00:03:19,933
We ask: if the generating station fails, what infrastructure is affected, and what

35
00:03:19,984 --> 00:03:24,736
should we prioritize? The commander runs the real cascade engine and the CP-SAT

36
00:03:24,786 --> 00:03:29,538
allocator, then reports population impact, affected assets and prioritized actions —

37
00:03:29,588 --> 00:03:34,340
with direct links into simulation, optimization and the twin.

38
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:40,800
Multi-scenario comparison runs two failure hypotheses side by side through the same

39
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:44,960
deterministic cascade mathematics. One column per scenario — and the AI layer adds a

40
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:49,120
plain-language trade-off analysis with twin highlights. Every number is computed by

41
00:03:49,170 --> 00:03:53,280
the platform; the language model only narrates it.

42
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:59,575
The Simulation Lab is where operators rehearse failures. We inject a fault at the

43
00:03:59,625 --> 00:04:03,570
generating station, then run the cascade: deterministic, seeded and reproducible —

44
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:07,565
each asset scored against its redundancy envelope. Previews run read-only; results

45
00:04:07,615 --> 00:04:11,560
replay later on the twin.

46
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:17,662
Incident management turns a failure into a tracked case. We file a high-severity

47
00:04:17,712 --> 00:04:21,465
incident for a water-treatment asset. The backend enforces one open incident per

48
00:04:21,515 --> 00:04:25,267
asset and category, validates every status transition, and records the full

49
00:04:25,317 --> 00:04:29,069
lifecycle from detection to resolution.

50
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:35,516
Now the recovery planner. We add demand for the failed asset and let OR-Tools CP-SAT

51
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:39,662
allocate resources under real constraints — crews, materials, mobilisation and

52
00:04:39,711 --> 00:04:43,807
priority. The solver returns a fully explained allocation or proves the problem

53
00:04:43,858 --> 00:04:47,954
infeasible; it never guesses. The plan persists with its objective value and solver

54
00:04:48,004 --> 00:04:52,100
status.

55
00:04:54,449 --> 00:04:58,673
Every plan ships with explainable recovery intelligence: why each assignment was

56
00:04:58,723 --> 00:05:02,946
made, which resources were limiting, and alternatives the solver itself proved

57
00:05:02,996 --> 00:05:07,219
feasible. Explanations must match the solver's actual numbers.

58
00:05:09,569 --> 00:05:13,794
Resource management tracks crews, equipment and materials with statuses, home zones

59
00:05:13,844 --> 00:05:18,069
and costs — the inventory the allocator draws from.

60
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:24,459
Dispatch turns approved plans into repair tasks. Object-level authorization means an

61
00:05:24,509 --> 00:05:28,549
engineer can only ever see the tasks assigned to them.

62
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:35,870
Recovery workflows orchestrate the full chain — detection, allocation, reservation,

63
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:40,889
dispatch, repair, verification — as audited steps with idempotent retries.

64
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:47,040
The Resilience Intelligence report summarizes structural risk from live records:

65
00:05:47,090 --> 00:05:50,890
dependency hotspots, redundancy gaps and zone exposure — computed by the platform,

66
00:05:50,939 --> 00:05:54,740
with any AI layer strictly grounded.

67
00:05:57,090 --> 00:06:01,210
Analytics completes the picture with response times, task throughput and utilization

68
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:05,380
trends — all exportable for reporting. The numbers come from stored incidents, tasks

69
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:09,550
and reservations: measured, not estimated.

70
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,965
Notifications keep every role informed as incidents escalate and recoveries

71
00:06:14,015 --> 00:06:16,080
complete.

72
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:22,904
Administration closes the loop: user management, a role and permission matrix, and a

73
00:06:22,954 --> 00:06:27,429
complete audit log — who did what, when, and with what outcome.

74
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:33,990
Finally, the platform documents its own model assumptions and limits. Aurora Vale is

75
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:38,250
synthetic — and the product says so, everywhere it matters.

76
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:45,730
SYMBIOTIC CITY. Infrastructure fails in chains. Recovery should be planned that way.

